---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import { Card, Badge } from "webcoreui/astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
import WipAlert from "@components/WipAlert.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Project Roadmap & Open-Source Ecosystem - Replenish Guide"
    description="Explore how this comprehensive Premodern Replenish strategic primer evolves as an open-source collaborative ecosystem, view upcoming pedagogical tools in our backlog, and learn how to contribute."
>
    <PageHeader
        title="Project & Roadmap"
        description="Discover our open-source architecture, initiate tactical discussions in the Discord ecosystem, suggest targeted additions, and track our ongoing pedagogical engineering backlog."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/tomb.webp"
        imageAlt="Ancient Tomb"
        imageCaption="Ancient Tomb by Colin MacNeil"
        isCard={true}
    />

    <WipAlert />

    <Card title="An Open-Source & Community-Driven Ecosystem" titleTag="h2">
        <p
            style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-20); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
        >
            This strategic compendium is not a static article; it is a <strong
                >living, collaborative, open-source repository</strong
            > maintained by and for the Premodern Magic community. As metagames adapt,
            new sideboard concepts emerge, and tricky stack physics refine, this guide
            relies on shared player rigor to remain the definitive resource for Replenish
            pilots.
        </p>
        <div
            style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;"
        >
            <div
                style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
            >
                <strong
                    style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem;"
                    >1. Strategic & Tournament Feedback</strong
                >
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Share tournament match reports, propose sideboard adjustments,
                    or debate mulligan heuristics by initiating conversations within
                    the <strong>Premodern Replenish Discord</strong> community.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div
                style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
            >
                <strong
                    style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem;"
                    >2. Feature & Material Requests</strong
                >
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Notice an unaddressed matchup, an omitted anti-graveyard tech
                    card, or a complex priority loop ruling? Open an <strong
                        >Issue on GitHub</strong
                    > to suggest targeted additions or supplementary learning material.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div
                style="background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--w-md-radius); border-left: 3px solid var(--w-color-primary-40);"
            >
                <strong
                    style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem;"
                    >3. Code & UI Contributions</strong
                >
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Built with <strong>Astro and TypeScript</strong>, our web architecture
                    invites frontend developers to claim tasks directly from our
                    engineering backlog—submitting Pull Requests to expand tools
                    and refine UX aesthetics.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </Card>

    <Card title="Project Backlog & Strategic Roadmap" titleTag="h2">
        <p
            style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-20); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;"
        >
            With our foundational UX architecture—including modular <code
                >&lt;MatchupCard&gt;</code
            > visual layouts, tiered sideboard categorizations, and exhaustive hate-counterplay
            deep dives—now fully implemented, this guide continues to evolve as a
            living tactical repository. Our active backlog highlights upcoming pedagogical
            tooling and strategic expansions:
        </p>
        <ul
            style="padding-left: 0; list-style: none; margin-bottom: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;"
        >
            <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.15rem;">
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>In Planning</Badge>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                        >Interactive Mulligan Sandbox & Hand Simulator:</strong
                    > Developing an in-browser interactive hand generator to test
                    decision heuristics against specific format archetypes and simulated
                    pre-game disruption.
                </div>
            </li>
            <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.15rem;">
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>
                        Open for Contribution
                    </Badge>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                        >Tournament Quick-Reference "Cheat Sheet":</strong
                    > Creating a condensed, single-screen or printable pocket summary
                    detailing sideboard In/Out matrices and Intuition selection packages
                    for fast round-to-round tournament reference.
                </div>
            </li>
            <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.15rem;">
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>
                        Active Maintenance
                    </Badge>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                        >Ongoing Post-Ban Metagame Evolutions:</strong
                    > Periodically re-calibrating sideboard flex slots, threat assessments,
                    and archetype badges as contemporary regional championship meta
                    dynamics shift.
                </div>
            </li>
            <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.15rem;">
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>
                        Open for Contribution
                    </Badge>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                        >Changelog & Version Architecture:</strong
                    > Integrating a user-facing release feed to transparently document
                    rules updates, newly introduced matchups, and primer revisions
                    over time.
                </div>
            </li>
            <li style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.15rem;">
                    <Badge theme="secondary" small={true}>In Development</Badge>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong style="color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                        >Video Match Post-Mortems & Replay Archive:</strong
                    > Integrating curated championship match recordings and turn-by-turn
                    video breakdowns illustrating complex stack manipulations in live
                    competitive environments.
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Card>
    <DecklistTooltip />
</Layout>
